.TH SDL_HINT_SCREENSAVER_INHIBIT_ACTIVITY_NAME 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_SCREENSAVER_INHIBIT_ACTIVITY_NAME \- Specify an \(dqactivity name\(dq for screensaver inhibition.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_SCREENSAVER_INHIBIT_ACTIVITY_NAME \(dqSDL_SCREENSAVER_INHIBIT_ACTIVITY_NAME\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Some platforms, notably Linux desktops, list the applications which are inhibiting the screensaver or other power-saving features\[char46]
.PP
This hint lets you specify the \(dqactivity name\(dq sent to the OS when
.BR SDL_DisableScreenSaver ()
is used (or the screensaver is automatically disabled)\[char46] The contents of this hint are used when the screensaver is disabled\[char46] You should use a string that describes what your program is doing (and, therefore, why the screensaver is disabled)\[char46] For example, \(dqPlaying a game\(dq or \(dqWatching a video\(dq\[char46]
.PP
Setting this to \(dq\(dq or leaving it unset will have SDL use a reasonable default: \(dqPlaying a game\(dq or something similar\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before calling
.BR SDL_DisableScreenSaver ()

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

